  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 104.79 Universal waste handler",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 104.79 “Universal waste handler” means:\n\n(a) A generator of universal waste; or\n\n(b) The owner or operator of a facility, including all contiguous property, who:\n\n(1) Receives universal waste from other universal waste handlers;\n\n(2) Accumulates universal waste; or\n\n(3) Sends universal waste to another universal waste handler, a destination facility, or a foreign destination.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Hw 100) #12343, eff 8-14-17; (formerly Env-Hw 104.73, renumbered by #13405) (See Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-Hw 100) (formerly Env-Hw 104.77)",
